# WARP-8: Steps on the kit shows the picked drum's lane: a bar a step's velocity, its chance under it, its ratchets,
# a dot where it holds locks; the other drums thin beneath. (The eleven lanes' grid is HOME's)
wait 300
listen
expect trk 1
expect page Steps
# the snare on 5 and 13, a hat on every other step
tapkey b1
tapkey w4
tapkey w12
tapkey b2
tapkey w0
tapkey w2
tapkey w4
tapkey w6
tapkey w8
tapkey w10
tapkey w12
tapkey w14
# the kick: steps 1, 5, 9, 12, 15
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
tapkey w8
tapkey w11
tapkey w14
# step 5 quieter
key w4 down
wait 100
turn K1 -50
wait 40
key w4 up
# step 9: a chance of 60%
key w8 down
wait 100
turn K3 60
wait 40
key w8 up
# step 12: in a fill only
key w11 down
wait 100
turn K3 200
turn K3 -1
wait 40
key w11 up
# step 15: three ratchets (ARP: its tricks)
key w14 down
wait 100
tap ARP
turn K1 3
turn K2 -9
turn K2 2
wait 40
key w14 up
# step 1: a lock from EDIT
tap EDIT
key w0 down
wait 100
turn K3 5
wait 40
key w0 up
tap SEQ
wait 60
expect page Steps
shot lane.png
key w8 down
wait 200
shot lane_held.png
key w8 up
